{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1527787-where-does-the-word-yozi-come-from","id":1527787,"title":"Where does the word yozi come from?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-02T14:30:27-08:00","id":1527787,"title":"Where does the word yozi come from?","content":"What religion/mythology does that word come from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27683-bernese","name":"Bernese","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-02T15:31:20-08:00","id":1527790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bernese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1527787-where-does-the-word-yozi-come-from#post1527787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What religion/mythology does that word come from?</div> </div> </div> </div>The word comes from <a href=\"https://sacred-texts.com/neu/dun/tago/tago07.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><b><i>Time and the Gods</i></b></a>, second book of the Pegana series by Lord Dunsany, one of the founders of the fantasy genre as we know it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-02T19:50:18-08:00","id":1527807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1527787-where-does-the-word-yozi-come-from?p=1527790#post1527790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The word comes from <a href=\"https://sacred-texts.com/neu/dun/tago/tago07.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><b><i>Time and the Gods</i></b></a>, second book of the Pegana series by Lord Dunsany, one of the founders of the fantasy genre as we know it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. The word, surprisingly, is from English. It's a fantasy made-up word, but still an English origin one.<br /> <br /> The original story can be found here:<br /> <a href=\"https://sacred-texts.com/neu/dun/tago/tago07.htm\" target=\"_blank\">https://sacred-texts.com/neu/dun/tago/tago07.htm</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member